      "message": "[warning] Line 112: 🟡 Size-capped downloads are aborted via `reply-\u003eabort()`, but `finished` maps every non-`NoError` to `NETWORK_ERROR`. This turns an intentional policy reject (oversize clipboard image) into a generic network failure signal. Handle `QNetworkReply::OperationCanceledError` caused by max-size enforcement separately (ignore or emit a dedicated/canceled status) so callers and UI can distinguish policy limits from real transport errors.",
